\define config-title() $:/config/cypro/DevMode

<!--
  Developer-mode toggle
  =====================

  A single click flips the whole UI between the END-USER perspective (for
  distribution / printing / daily use) and the DEVELOPER perspective (for editing
  the plugin's source tiddlers).

  The button manages FOUR config states together. Turning it on sets all of them to
  "yes", turning it off sets all to "no", so the UI can never be left in an
  inconsistent half-state (e.g. when switching back to normal view before an export).

  Controlled states:

  1. $:/config/cypro/DevMode
     When "yes", styles/layout stops hiding the cypro ViewTemplates for tiddlers
     tagged KIKS / threat / measure / form / help / navigation / tutorial and shows
     the raw TW view (title, tags, body) so the underlying tiddlers can be edited.

  2. $:/view
     Set to "classic" (several tiddlers visible at once, classic story-river view) or
     back to "zoomin" (focus on a single tiddler — the cypro UI's default).

  3. $:/config/cypro/ShowOriginalSidebar
     When "yes", styles/layout shows TiddlyWiki's standard sidebar — the search box
     and the Open/Recent/Tools/More tabs — above the cypro sidebar. When "no" only the
     cypro sidebar remains.

  4. $:/config/cypro/ShowOriginalPageControls
     When "yes", styles/layout shows all the standard page-control buttons (save, home,
     control panel, manager, new tiddler, import, export, etc.). The cypro buttons
     (new-kiks, dev-mode, print, help) carry the class cypro-toolbar-btn, which is how
     the CSS tells them apart from the standard ones.

  Important for distribution:
  The shipped state is "all flags = no / $:/view = zoomin". In that state the exported
  TiddlyWiki file shows only the cypro UI — no original sidebar, no original toolbar,
  no raw ViewTemplates. So always make sure the toggle is OFF before exporting.
-->

<$button
    tooltip="Entwickler-Modus"
    aria-label="Entwickler-Modus"
    class={{{
        [[tc-btn-invisible ]]
        [<tv-config-toolbar-class>]
        [[cypro-toolbar-btn]]
        [<config-title>get[text]match[yes]then[tc-selected]]
        +[join[ ]]
    }}}
>
    <!--
      Order matters: set DevMode LAST so the first three actions still read the OLD
      value. Otherwise actions 2-4 would already read the newly-set DevMode and run
      inverted.
    -->
    <$action-setfield
        $tiddler="$:/config/cypro/ShowOriginalSidebar"
        text={{{ [<config-title>get[text]match[yes]then[no]else[yes]] }}}
    />
    <$action-setfield
        $tiddler="$:/config/cypro/ShowOriginalPageControls"
        text={{{ [<config-title>get[text]match[yes]then[no]else[yes]] }}}
    />
    <$action-setfield
        $tiddler="$:/view"
        text={{{ [<config-title>get[text]match[yes]then[zoomin]else[classic]] }}}
    />
    <$action-setfield
        $tiddler=<<config-title>>
        text={{{ [<config-title>get[text]match[yes]then[no]else[yes]] }}}
    />
    <span class={{{ [<config-title>get[text]match[yes]then[cypro-devmode-active]] }}}>
        {{$:/core/images/theme-button}}
    </span>
</$button>